# Periodic noise on a 256x128 canvas. Every cell draws one wrapped tile several times edge to edge, and the copies join with no seam: no line, step, or repeated edge where tiles meet.
# Top row, left to right, four 64x64 cells of a 32x32 tile drawn in a 2x2 grid, each with wrap:32 and seed:1 through the blue ramp: simplex (winding blobs), perlin (soft blobs), worley (round bright cells with dark seams), value (soft low-contrast blobs).
# Each top cell shows the same 32x32 pattern four times, so the top-left quarter of a cell matches its other three quarters exactly.
# Bottom row, left to right: fbm(simplex(16 wrap:64)) through the gold ramp, one 64x64 tile drawn twice side by side; ridged(worley(16 wrap:64,32)) through the red ramp, a 64x32 tile drawn in a 2x2 grid.
# The bottom-left pair reads as one 128x64 grainy texture whose right half equals its left half. The bottom-right cell repeats a 64-wide, 32-tall pattern, so its halves match left to right and top to bottom.
@target fields/wrap.png 256x128

def quad noise:value(8 wrap:32 seed:1)
  rect 32x32 at:-16,-16 fill:noise -> p.blue name:tl
  rect 32x32 at:16,-16 fill:noise -> p.blue name:tr
  rect 32x32 at:-16,16 fill:noise -> p.blue name:bl
  rect 32x32 at:16,16 fill:noise -> p.blue name:br

quad noise:simplex(8 wrap:32 seed:1) at:32,32 name:a
quad noise:perlin(8 wrap:32 seed:1) at:96,32 name:b
quad noise:worley(8 wrap:32 seed:1) at:160,32 name:c
quad noise:value(8 wrap:32 seed:1) at:224,32 name:d

rect 64x64 at:32,96 fill:fbm(simplex(16 wrap:64 seed:2)) -> p.gold name:e
rect 64x64 at:96,96 fill:fbm(simplex(16 wrap:64 seed:2)) -> p.gold name:f
rect 64x32 at:160,80 fill:ridged(worley(16 wrap:64,32 seed:3)) -> p.red name:g
rect 64x32 at:224,80 fill:ridged(worley(16 wrap:64,32 seed:3)) -> p.red name:h
rect 64x32 at:160,112 fill:ridged(worley(16 wrap:64,32 seed:3)) -> p.red name:i
rect 64x32 at:224,112 fill:ridged(worley(16 wrap:64,32 seed:3)) -> p.red name:j
